# Legacy (old AI-generated code kept as reference only)
/_legacy/

# Internal planning — working notes, closeouts, unreleased design docs, and
# anything held back from `docs/` for being stale. The private half of the pair
# below.
/plan/

# `docs/` is NOT ignored, and that is deliberate — read this before "fixing" it.
#
# `c67aef5` un-ignored `docs/` and `413d22b` reverted it, for a reason that was
# right: it published the entire working directory, stale drafts included, and
# two files had to be excluded by hand. That commit set the condition for doing
# it properly — anything the public repo needs gets *migrated* deliberately and
# "curated at that point."
#
# 2026-09-09 is that migration. The uncurated files moved to `plan/` first (the
# April PDF, and `gap_analysis.md`, which claimed score-2.0.0 M5–M7 were unbuilt
# after all of M1–M7 had landed). What remains is published documentation:
# `architecture.md` and `scoring_metric.md` — the latter being Tranche 3
# Deliverable 4 — plus the generated corpus report the README and PHASE_4 cite.
#
# So the invariant is one rule per directory, which is why there is no entry
# here: `docs/` is published and curated, `plan/` is the working area. A file
# that is not ready to be read by a stranger belongs in `plan/`, not behind a
# new ignore rule.

# Personal sandbox — kept locally for reference but not pushed.
# Test-relevant fixtures live in `samples/contracts/` instead.
/learning/

# CLI output defaults
/out/

# soroban-sdk's test host writes a JSON snapshot of every test's ledger, auth
# and event state next to the crate under test. Useful for eyeballing a probe
# run, but it is regenerated on every invocation and is not a golden file —
# committing it would produce churn on every `--ignored` run. When the harness
# grows real golden files (plan B7) they get an explicit, committed home.
**/test_snapshots/

